From: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: reserve higher bandwidth for HS periodic endpoints

Backport of Qualcomm's LKML Feb-2025 quirk ("usb: dwc3: Reserve Higher
Bandwidth for HS Periodic EPs"), made unconditional: the Dragon Q6A's
devicetree is bootloader-owned and cannot carry the upstream snps,*
quirk property, so the DT gate is dropped and the bit is set for every
DWC3 revision >= 250A.

The host controller reserves 80% of the bus for periodic endpoints by
default; with GUCTL bit 16 set the reservation relaxes to 85%, which is
what two high-bandwidth isochronous endpoints need (two 1024x3-per-
microframe UVC cameras ~= 82%). Motivation: multiple UVC cameras on the
QCM6490's DWC3 controllers failed VIDIOC_STREAMON with ENOSPC ("Not
enough bandwidth for altsetting 1") whenever a second camera started on
the same controller; one camera per controller worked.

Signed-off-by: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
index dfa1b5fe48dc..7e55c234e4e5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
@@ -418,6 +418,7 @@
 /* Global User Control Register*/
 #define DWC3_GUCTL_REFCLKPER_MASK		0xffc00000
 #define DWC3_GUCTL_REFCLKPER_SEL		22
+#define DWC3_GUCTL_RESBWHSEPS			BIT(16)
 
 /* Global User Control Register 2 */
 #define DWC3_GUCTL2_RST_ACTBITLATER		BIT(14)
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
index dfa1b5fe48dc..7e55c234e4e5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -1480,6 +1480,20 @@ static int dwc3_core_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 		dwc3_writel(dwc->regs, DWC3_GUCTL1, reg);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Relax the host controller's periodic-endpoint bandwidth
+	 * reservation from 80% to 85% of the bus (GUCTL bit 16): two
+	 * high-bandwidth isochronous endpoints (e.g. two UVC cameras at
+	 * 1024x3 per microframe, ~= 82%) then fit on one controller.
+	 * Set unconditionally — the upstream DT property gate is
+	 * unusable here because the devicetree is bootloader-owned.
+	 */
+	if (dwc->revision >= DWC3_REVISION_250A) {
+		reg = dwc3_readl(dwc->regs, DWC3_GUCTL);
+		reg |= DWC3_GUCTL_RESBWHSEPS;
+		dwc3_writel(dwc->regs, DWC3_GUCTL, reg);
+	}
+
 	dwc3_config_threshold(dwc);
 
 	/*
